The Latin font file referenced there (<https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/inter/v12/UcCO3FwrK3iLTeHuS_fvQtMwCp50KnMw2boKoduKmMEVuLyfAZ9hiJ-Ek-_EeA.woff2>) has SHA-1 hash `4ddb25ec1c4250101c1a8371911a9efc80ca64df`, whereas that of the file you are currently serving (<https://spec.matrix.org/v1.4/fonts/Inter-latin-normal-400.woff2>) is `e42a5f249124b37caeb4501bf752ce73e83f5b31`.

***

And here is the response using Curl, without sending any HTTP headers such as User-Agent, which as you can see serves only the URL of a single TTF file (with SHA-1 hash `81da85b088cedc0617f800e1c7df2a236a063a70`), not a WOFF2 file:

```
$ curl -L 'https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Inter'
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Inter';
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400;
  src: url(https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/inter/v12/UcCO3FwrK3iLTeHuS_fvQtMwCp50KnMw2boKoduKmMEVuLyfAZ9hjQ.ttf) format('truetype');
}
```
